The file is a complete, well-disciplined conformance suite for `contracts/05-suggested-fix-registry.yaml` (`suggested-fix-registry/0.1.0`). Protocol, structure, epistemic tagging, fixture design, case inventory, and rule-coverage mapping all meet the manifest item's requirements. Spot-checked extractions verify against their cited sources. The file is acceptable with one cosmetic citation note; no revision is needed.

## Protocol compliance

- Raw deliverable (`runs/turn8-20/deliverables/turn12.md`) wraps content in a single fenced block annotated `markdown:conformance/05-suggested-fix-registry.md` with no content outside the fence except `<!-- TURN_END:12 -->`. Marker number matches the manifest item (12). Pass.
- File under review is the inner content only, ending at a coherent sign-off boundary (evidence bundle, sign-off gate, no-amendment statement). Not truncated. Pass.

## Completeness and structure

- Delivers what a conformance suite should: scope/acceptance boundary, deterministic runner and result discipline, assertion surfaces, validation layers, fixture construction (shared mechanics, `BASE-CF` graph, registration order, companion fixtures), organized test vectors (`S01–S04`, `H01–H06`, `J01–J05`, `V01–V02`, `C01–C03`, `R01–R04`, `E01–E08`, `P01–P11`, `T01–T06`, `A01–A07`), full `FIX-*` rule-coverage mapping, and evidence-bundle/sign-off requirements. Each vector states input/mutation plus required oracle. Pass.

## Epistemic discipline

- Every substantive paragraph/row carries an epistemic tag (`[extracted: …]`, `[inferred: …]`, or `[proposed: …]`). Proposed runner mechanics, oracle notation (`ACCEPT`/`REJECT`/`EMIT`/`WITHHOLD`), exit dispositions, and synthetic fixtures are explicitly marked as proposals or suite notation, never as extracted facts. The file repeatedly guards against overclaiming (e.g., §1 execution-status disclaimer, §2.1 runner as "implementation target", §2.2 labels as "suite notation, not additions to the registry wire schema", §3 synthetic-only evidence). Pass.

